stbusters you can watch that not even  get the jokes and I think that  particularly funny but there's still  stuff there you can latch on to some of  the other cell in the trail I can't  decide what I feel about the fact that  they're going for these I mean like that  there's a dragon ghost I can't decide  what I think about that there's part of  me that wants to say it's kind of stupid  but it's very reminiscent of the  Ghostbusters cartoon which is something  that i love but I mean that was a  cartoon it was for little little kids so  I don't I don't know it doesn't excite  me I'll say that much and I'm kind of  really annoyed that they showed us a  Kevin Chris Hemsworth getting possessed  and then showing a snippet that makes it  look pretty clear  like he is going to factor into the  climax like and somehow they're going to  have to take him down at the end and  whatever's possessing him is like part  of the really big thing it's not just  he's possessed oh we fix it we move on  which unfortunately makes it feel like  something that I'd complain about lately  with trailers they're giving away a big  chunk of the climax i think watching the  movie if this was a character that I  liked I don't know if I was gonna like  him or not but if it was and he then got  possessed and he's zooming off to help  the ghost and we're going to the climax  that could have really upped the tension  for the climax and the tension is about  the only thing I've got any hope for  left cuz as i said the action scenes  look okay but now i already know that's  going to happen i'm not as angry about  it because this isn't a movie i care as  much about both i would put this right  up there as being of the exact same  level of problem as spoiling the  wolverine reveal in the latest Xmen  apocalypse trailer or spoiling the  doomsday reveal in batman be superman  why our trailers doing this so part of  me wants to save the trailer slightly  better because like i said i'm able to  kind of hone 